                <pb facs="0253" n="127" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg127"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51 W 89Czechoslovakia/99: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Czechoslovakia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Einstein</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-07-16T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 16, 1925—5
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>28. Your 37, July 11, 1 P.M. On July 10 the following memorandum was handed to
                    Czechoslovak Chargé: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The World War Foreign Debt Commission would be glad to negotiate upon
                            the settlement of the entire Czechoslovak debt to the United States with
                            a commission from Czechoslovakia having due power to negotiate and
                            conclude a settlement. Arrangements could be made in the debt settlement
                            for an appropriate adjustment of any part of the total indebtedness not
                            now admitted by Czechoslovakia to be due. There is no reason, however,
                            why a debt settlement need await a verification of the total since this
                            is simply a mechanical <pb facs="0254" n="128" xml:id="pg128"/> matter
                            of auditing the accounts, and any debt settlement should cover the
                            entire debt whatever it is ultimately determined to be.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Please keep Department informed by telegraph of further developments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
